{"name":"Fresh Sawdust","hex":"#c8a278","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Newly produced or obtained; recent.","(of food) Not dried, frozen, or spoiled."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Recently; just recently; most recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh"},{"term":"sawdust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fine particles (dust) created by sawing wood or other material.","Food that is unpleasantly powdery and tasteless."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sprinkle with sawdust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sawdust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sawdust","blocks":[{"text":"Sawdust is a by-product or waste product of woodworking operations such as sawing, sanding, milling and routing. It is composed of very small chips of wood. These operations can be performed by woodworking machinery, portable power tools or by use of hand tools. In some manufacturing industries it can be a significant fire hazard and source of occupational dust exposure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Saw_dust_%28Zaagsel%29.jpg/330px-Saw_dust_%28Zaagsel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sawdust","wikidata":"Q816713"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg/500px-Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg/1280px-Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg/500px-Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki